 "notes": "Approximate digitization; not supplied or endorsed by FUJIFILM. All four page-8 charts are embedded 1-bit CCITT scans (about 600 dpi) with black curves on white; no vector curve paths. Every grid line was fitted as its own sloped line on the native image pixels and the axes were calibrated piecewise on those fitted lines. Spectral sensitivity and dye density curves were traced with a direction-following centreline tracker (frame lines removed, grid lines left in place and crossed). Characteristic curves (section 19): exposure 'Daylight,' (no exposure time printed), process E-6/CR-56, densitometry Status A; legend R solid, G long-dash, B short-dash. Above about D 3.0 (shoulder) the three curves are separate and were traced with the tracker (grid lines removed there, dash gaps and grid crossings linearly interpolated). Below about D 3.0 the three printed curves lie within one or two line widths of each other and merge into one ink band about 17 px (about 0.045 D) wide; there the band was profiled along its normal and the solid R line taken as the band's upper-right edge minus half the measured solid-line width (5.5 px), the dashed line as the opposite edge plus half that width; on the D-min plateau (log H above about 0.35) the dashes lie on top of the solid line and the sides were swapped (chosen there by edge roughness: the solid edge is the smooth one). Profile offsets were median-filtered along the curve. The long-dash G and short-dash B lines cannot be told apart in that band, so below about D 3.0 G and B are the same dashed trace; treat G-B differences there as unresolved and R-vs-G/B differences as uncertain by about +-0.015 D. Curves resampled every 0.02 log H. Small density rises were removed with a running minimum (largest change 0.0196 D, on the D-min plateau near log H 1.0 where the traced dashes sit on top of the solid line). Spectral sensitivity (section 20): process E-6/CR-56, densitometry Status A, density 1.0 above D-min; y axis 'Sensitivity* (log)' with ticks -1.0, 0.0, 1.0, 2.0, values recorded on that axis as charted; the near-vertical ends are sampled at 1 nm, and the last few pixels of the green curve's long-wavelength tail, which curl back by under 1 nm, are not representable as a function of wavelength and are dropped. Spectral dye density (section 22): exposure 'Separated', process E-6/CR-56; separate yellow, magenta and cyan curves recorded; the chart starts at about 380 nm; the yellow curve runs into the 0.0 axis line near 595 nm and is recorded only up to there. rms_granularity is the single printed Diffuse RMS Granularity Value (section 17: 9; 48 um aperture, sample density 1.0 above minimum density); no granularity curve is published. No reference exposure, 18% grey aim or normal-exposure mark is given anywhere in the bulletin, so no log_h_ref is recorded and x stays absolute log H. No mid-scale neutral or minimum-density spectral curve is published. Not recorded (no field in this schema): MTF curve (section 21), resolving power (80 lines/mm at 1.6:1, 160 lines/mm at 1000:1). viewing D50: the bulletin (section 10) asks for an ISO 3664:2000 transparency viewer, CIE illuminant D50, 5000 K.",
